      "writtenOn": "2025-03-14T08:14:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "During my testing, I found that when using aggressive initial parameters, L2CA_UpdateBleConnParams may be called by L2CA_SetEcosystemBaseInterval() also with the aggressive parameter.\nIf reset \u0027L2C_BLE_AGGRESSIVE_INITIAL_PARAM\u0027 here, when calling L2CA_LockBleConnParamsForProfileConnection()\n to unlock the parameters, it will not update to the relaxed parameters for the flag is reset.\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/stack/l2cap/l2c_ble_conn_params.cc;l\u003d299\n\nSo I add the condition \u0027max_int \u003e LeConnectionParameters::GetMaxConnIntervalAggressive()\u0027.\nIf max_int \u003c\u003d LeConnectionParameters::GetMaxConnIntervalAggressive(), that means, this calling is also use the aggressive parameters. we shouldn\u0027t reset the \u0027L2C_BLE_AGGRESSIVE_INITIAL_PARAM\u0027 flag.",
      "parentUuid": "b2fbc08c_28898fdd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 92,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 94,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "3d9565ea6369f7f9d4ee956ce5e9d65c13300a61",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "02ee4b0e_b03bddf5",
        "filename": "system/stack/l2cap/l2c_ble_conn_params.cc",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 94,
      "author": {
        "id": 1112679
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-14T08:40:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`L2CA_LockBleConnParamsForProfileConnection(false)` is used for going back to the requested conn. param values. Therefore if `L2CA_UpdateBleConnParams` is called then the values should be the ones when unlock happens.\n\nHow about calling `L2CA_UpdateBleConnParams` with the relaxed value at some point? That unlock will naturally change the param go back to relaxed mode.",
      "parentUuid": "0e669329_c58d3725",
